1b:["$","p","1",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"On the GED, the extended response is not an opinion essay. You read two passages that take opposite sides of an issue and explain which argument is better supported by evidence. Your own view of the topic is not being assessed and does not earn points. What earns points is a clear position, evidence drawn from the passages, and organized, readable prose. If you are taking a different exam, read its own rubric, because the task may differ."}]
