hildren":"Because it was late."}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Attach it to a main clause"}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Pronoun agreement"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Each student brought their book"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Acceptable now; older tests may prefer his or her"}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Confusable words"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"their / there / they're"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Learn the three; they appear constantly"}]]}],["$","tr","5",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Shifting tense"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"She walked in and sits down"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Keep one tense"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"Grammar errors the test checks most"}]]}]
1f:["$","$L24","5",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"The extended response asks which of two arguments is better supported. You strongly disagree with the better-supported one. What should you write?","options":["Argue for the position you agree with — sincerity scores well","Argue that the better-supported argument is better supported, using evidence from the passages","Argue both sides equally and let the reader decide","Explain why the question itself is flawed"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"The task is analytical, not persuasive. You are assessed on whether you can identify and demonstrate which argument the evidence supports — your own agreement is not part of the rubric, and substituting it means answering a different question.","optionRationales":["Your view is not what is being scored, however sincerely held.","Correct. Answer the question asked, using the passages as evidence.","Refusing to take a position loses points on Trait 1, creating an argument and using evidence, which is the heart of the task.","This does not answer the prompt at all."]}}]
